8. NMR Algorithm and Real‑Time Technical Specification

8.1 Complete Control Loop

Algorithm 1: NMR Self‑Stabilising Control Loop

```  
Require: nominal controller π_nom, behavior repertoire B = {(d_k, π_k)}, 
         pre‑trained Lipschitz GNN F_φ, hyperparameters w_max, h_min, β, λ,
         adaptation gains Γ, K_d, Λ, watchdog threshold τ_thresh, timer T_watchdog

Initialize: residual network ψ = ψ_0 (meta‑learned),
           adaptive estimate θ̂ = θ_0, sliding buffer for inverse model

Loop at 1 kHz:
  // Phase 1: Health Perception (1–2 ms)
  Read raw diagnostics → local health h_i(t) via Eq(3)
  Form node features f_i = [h_i, ḣ_i, τ_i^err, ε_i, ...]
  Forward pass Lipschitz GNN → h^global   (Eq 4, ≤3 ms)

  // Phase 2: Behavior Selection (sporadic, <1 ms)
  if performance drops below threshold:
      Compute similarity(h^global, d_k) for all k
      if max similarity > γ: set π_nom ← best‑matching π_k

  // Phase 3: Torque Computation (≈1 ms)
  Determine active joint set S (exclude joints with h_i ≈ 0)
  τ_wqp = solve health‑weighted QP (5) using W(h^global), active constraints
  τ_res = Δπ_ψ(x, h^global)   (residual forward pass, <0.5 ms)
  τ_cmd = τ_wqp + τ_res
  Apply box clipping to τ_cmd

  // Phase 4: Bistable Joint Mode Control
  foreach joint with bistable mode:
      if h_i < h_critical: set mode = SOFT else RIGID

  // Phase 5: Safety Watchdog
  if ||τ_res|| > τ_thresh for >200 ms:
      disable Δπ_ψ, revert to Lyapunov controller (11) only

  // Phase 6: Apply torques and modes to actuators

  // Background Tasks (asynchronous)
  Every 50 ms:
      Update inverse dynamics model f̂⁻¹ via Ridge on recent buffer
      Compute gradient via Eq(10) and perform one Adam step on ψ (lr=1e‑3)
  Every 500 ms:
      Update θ̂ using composite law (14) discretized via Euler
```

